# @epistemologic/cybernetic/viable — Beer 1972/1979/1984. The
# substrate-altitude declaration of the Viable System Model species:
# identity-preservation under environmental disturbance. The first
# species on Track A that does NOT inherit from eigenform — it
# INSTANTIATES the parametric carrier directly with a non-trivial ω.
#
# Per the spec at `docs/specs/cyberpunk-viable.md` (Mara `9154d6b` on
# `reed/recursion-lock-tower-audit`; 1230 lines), this shard is the
# substrate landing of:
#
# - Reading A held (homeostat): T_reg = Identity, T_regd = Stability,
#   τ : Identity ↔ Stability via Ashby's homeostat law.
# - Reading B held (recursive viability): the parent S5 over child
#   viable systems; inheritance read as the recursive descent of the
#   parametric carrier.
# - Reading C does not hold: the S3-S4 oscillation IS captured by the
#   contraction-surface dynamics; the parametric form is not refused.
# - Reading D held (the temporal lock surfaced during the audit): the
#   first species in the audit to carry a NON-TRIVIAL ω. Read D
#   instantiates the parametric carrier's `omega` field with the
#   temporal-identity Δt-window (per coherence-parametric's connection_form
#   `is_trivial: false` slot, the slot coevolution and viable share).
#
# === Why this is the first non-eigenform-inheritor species ===
#
# Distinction (the floor) and second_order (the ceiling) BOTH inherit
# from eigenform per §8.8.1 — re-entry IS eigenform; the reflexive
# turn IS eigenform; one ancestor with two inheritors at the floor
# and ceiling of @cyberpunk.
#
# Viable does NOT need fixed-point machinery at its altitude. Its
# inheritance points are different:
#
# - From `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`: the
#   (T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω) lock_pair carrier; viable INSTANTIATES this
#   with (Identity, Stability, ρ_regular, ω_temporal).
# - From `@epistemologic/cybernetic/variety`: the variety_vector axes;
#   viable's S3/S4 oscillation IS Ashby variety-matching at the VSM
#   altitude; the bilateral predicate the consumer pulls discharges
#   `variety_preserving` at the species' boundary alongside the
#   parametric lock witness.
# - From `@epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order`: the canonical ρ
#   choice. Per the spec §3.5 + the parametric carrier's docs §8.7:
#   viable's regulator/regulated read at altitude α+1 IS a second-
#   order observation of the system observing itself maintaining
#   identity; the regular rep on L²(𝒢) the second_order shard
#   declares IS the ρ viable's lock_pair carries. The substrate-pull
#   here: viable does not RE-DECLARE ρ; it INHERITS the regular rep
#   from second_order and instantiates the parametric carrier with
#   that ρ.
#
# Three inheritance points, no eigenform. The species' shape is the
# instantiation, not the fixed-point closure.
#
# === Read A (homeostat) carriers, verbatim from spec §3.1 ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the system's S5 *policy*; holds identity-
#   constraints (the survival-bound predicate).
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the S1-S4 *operational layers*; the units
#   doing variety-production under disturbance.
# - T_reg = `Identity` — the substrate-altitude carrier for *what
#   the system is*. Per [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]]
#   property #9, identity IS eigenform at the substrate altitude
#   (the per-shard identity vector, the Pack-altitude identity
#   carrier, or the SpectralUuid at the spectral-coordinate
#   altitude). At viable's altitude the identity surfaces as the
#   S5 policy declaration; consumers compose with eigenform's
#   `identity_from_fixed` when they need the verified reading.
# - T_regd = `Stability` — the substrate-altitude carrier for
#   *whether the system maintains identity under disturbance*. A
#   transparency-shaped verdict reading `success` /
#   `partial(opacity_map)` / `failure(opacity_map)` per holonomy.md
#   §5 verdict family.
# - τ : Identity ↔ Stability — the natural substitution between
#   identity-as-policy and stability-as-operational-fact. A system
#   with identity `i` has stability `s = stability_of(i)` under
#   the homeostat reading. Read off by *running the system*
#   through a disturbance.
#
# Reading A's structural claim: stability IS what identity-
# preservation MEANS at the operational altitude. The substitution
# is natural because the homeostat law (Ashby 1952) says the
# system's stability under disturbance IS its identity surviving
# the disturbance.
#
# === Read D (temporal lock) carriers ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the system's identity-policy at time t.
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the system's identity-policy at time t+Δt.
# - T_reg = `Identity_t` — identity at one time-slice.
# - T_regd = `Identity_{t+Δt}` — identity at the next time-slice
#   (after the system has weathered disturbance over Δt).
# - τ : Identity_t ↔ Identity_{t+Δt} — the natural substitution
#   between time-slices via the system's regulation.
#
# Reads A and D are NOT in conflict; they are the parametric form
# at two altitudes of viable. The substrate carrier here surfaces
# BOTH via the non-trivial ω: ω carries the temporal-identity
# Δt-window per Read D; the (T_reg, T_regd) static pair carries
# the Read A homeostat.
#
# === The substrate's existing VSM-conformance ===
#
# Per spec §2.3 + [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]] §6, the
# substrate's three-tier stack ALREADY maps to a VSM at substrate
# altitude:
#
# - S1 (operations)              = fragmentation-mcp
# - S2 / S3 (coordination / mgmt) = mirror + SpectralSupervisor
# - S4 (intelligence / strategy)  = @spectral/db
# - S5 (identity / policy)        = the Pack identity layer
#                                   (Reed/Mara/Glint/Taut/Seam)
#
# The substrate has been *running* as a viable system since the
# three-tier stack architecture landed. This shard doesn't
# introduce viability; it names what the substrate has already
# been doing. ~67th instance of
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]].
#
# === Recursive viability (Read B) ===
#
# Per spec §3.2 + Beer 1972 ch. 10: every S1 is itself a viable
# system. The recursion is structural. The parametric form's
# `regulator_at(α+1)` over `regulated_at(α+1)` reads naturally as
# "the parent viable system's S5 regulating the child viable
# system" — the recursion is *in* the model, not added to it.
#
# At the substrate altitude: the Pack S5 (Reed/Mara/Glint/Taut/Seam)
# carries OuterViable; each member of the Pack carries InnerViable
# at their own altitude; each member is themselves a viable system
# (with their own S1-S5 internally). The recursive embedding IS
# the substitution τ : OuterViable ↔ InnerViable. Both are S5-shaped;
# Beer's recursive viability law guarantees naturality.
#
# Recursive viability is NOT re-declared here as a separate carrier:
# it lives in the parametric carrier's altitude field (the
# `lock_carrier.altitude` slot per coherence-parametric.mirror), with
# adjacent altitudes recording the parent/child pair.
#
# === Bundle-tower cross-reference (docs/math/the-tower/beam-runtime.md §5) ===
#
# The Beer VSM S1-S5 naming below maps onto the bundle tower's altitude
# structure at the runtime altitude per Mara `610c6d6` beam-runtime.md §5:
#
#   S1 (operations)              = @spectral/gen_prism (bundle sections
#                                   at BEAM/process altitude; each S1 is
#                                   itself viable per Beer 1972 ch.10 =
#                                   tower recursion)
#   S2 (coordination)            = @dance ensemble coordination (forward-
#                                   promised; Kuramoto phase-lock at
#                                   ensemble altitude = connection 1-form
#                                   at level k+1)
#   S3 (audit / management)      = @spectral/supervisor with restart_strategy
#                                   (connection at supervision altitude)
#   S4 (intelligence / strategy) = @spectral/db (psychohistory carrier)
#   S5 (identity / policy)       = viable.identity below + Pack S5
#                                   (Reed/Mara/Glint/Taut/Seam)
#
# Beer's recursive-viability law (viability_law(v) below at line 554) IS
# the bundle-tower's compatibility condition at S1-within-S1 altitude,
# same theorem as Baez-Schreiber 2004 pullback-agreement condition, two
# names for the same structural fact. See docs/specs/gen-prism-as-bundle-
# section-and-dance-as-ensemble-connection.md (Mara `fee2727`) for the
# canonical spec grounding the runtime-altitude naming in bundle-tower
# vocabulary.
#
# === Cybersyn as substrate-political analogue ===
#
# Per spec §2.4 + Mara `7807a77` SEL spec §2.5: Project Cybersyn
# (Chile, 1971-1973) was VSM deployed at the political-economic
# altitude. The Cybernet telegraph network routed S1-S5 channels
# over a national economy; the system was built to defend Chilean
# independence against external disturbance. The viability law:
# the Chilean economy IS a viable system iff the S1-S5 channels
# can maintain Chilean economic identity through external
# disturbance.
#
# The substrate-political continuity to SEL (Mara `7807a77` §2.5):
# the substrate's anti-extraction posture is structurally the same
# shape as Cybersyn's anti-imperialism posture; the *viability*
# species is what both deployments are protecting. SEL is the
# license-boundary lock that ENFORCES viability against extraction;
# viable is the identity-preservation lock that NAMES what is being
# protected.
#
# === The third-witness-gate question (spec §3.5; pending Alex) ===
#
# Per spec §3.5 the audit defaults to Gate-refined: viable closes
# the third witness IFF the math doc's §7 gate is reformulated in
# terms of axis-differentiation (scope, temporal, recursion-level,
# parallel-operation-pair) rather than scope-hierarchy. Forward-
# promised update at the spec §8 (recursion-locks.md §7 refinement
# pending Alex ratification). This shard lands the species at the
# substrate altitude; the gate verdict is the math-doc tick, not
# this one.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per cybernetic foundation §4.1, viable's seam maps to four
# cybernetic distinctions simultaneously:
#
# - von Foerster first/second-order: the system observes itself
#   maintaining identity through disturbance; the algedonic signal
#   (Beer 1979 ch. 6) IS the second-order alarm that the
#   first-order channels are damping a threat to identity. Per
#   spec §10 substrate-already-had-the-word item 6: @cyberpunk/
#   algedonic IS this signal at substrate altitude.
# - Maturana structure/organisation: viability IS the persistence
#   of organisation across structural perturbation. The system's
#   organisation IS its identity; the structural perturbation IS
#   the environmental disturbance.
# - Beer S3/S4: viable carries ALL FIVE VSM subsystems; the S3-S4
#   oscillation IS the homeostat reading at the operational
#   altitude per spec §3.3 case-against-Read-C.
# - Pask M/P-individual: a viable system's S5 IS the M-individual
#   it agrees with itself about; the recursive descent IS the
#   M-individual / P-individual partition replicating across
#   altitude.
#
# Four traditions converging at one carrier. The substrate runs
# all four at once at the viable altitude.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/viable`
# operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate ALREADY
# has the operational machinery (the three-tier stack IS the VSM
# at substrate altitude; the Pack-orchestra ratification at S5 IS
# Read A's regulator-at-altitude-α+1 operation); the property at
# this altitude names the carrier and the lock-pair instantiation
# so downstream shards can declare
# `requires viable_well_formed(my_system)` rather than restate the
# viability obligation in each species.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word density (per spec §10) ===
#
# Per spec §10, viable's vocabulary was almost entirely already
# implicit in the substrate. Seven named instances:
#
# 1. The three-tier stack IS VSM at the substrate altitude. See
#    spec §2.3 and [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]] §6.
# 2. eigenform IS the identity carrier (T_reg). Per
#    [[architecture-cybernetic-foundation]] property #9; viable's
#    T_reg IS eigenform's witness at the species altitude.
# 3. The Pack IS S5. See [[project-pack-is-orchestra]] and
#    [[architecture-peer-learns-by-crystal-vocabulary-expansion]].
# 4. The kintsugi loop IS the contraction surface. The
#    Polyak-Łojasiewicz contraction of identity-loss under
#    regulation lives in the existing kintsugi machinery; viable
#    names the species' instantiation.
# 5. transparency<p> IS the verdict carrier. The Stability carrier
#    here surfaces against the existing transparency family; no
#    new verdict type required.
# 6. @cyberpunk/algedonic IS the emergency signal. The S1→S5
#    bypass when first-order channels would damp a threat; the
#    sibling species at the family-root altitude per spec §2.1.
# 7. Cybersyn IS the political deployment. Spec §2.4; the
#    substrate-political precedent SEL lifted as analogue.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Beer 1972         (Brain of the Firm; Wiley) — the VSM
#                     introduction; S1-S5 structure; the original
#                     "viable system" naming; ch. 10 the recursive
#                     viability claim.
#   Beer 1979         (The Heart of Enterprise; Wiley) — the VSM
#                     elaboration; the recursive viability
#                     principle; S3 audit channel; the algedonic
#                     signal (ch. 6).
#   Beer 1984         ("The Viable System Model: Its Provenance,
#                     Development, Methodology and Pathology",
#                     Journal of the Operational Research Society
#                     35(1): 7-25) — the methodology paper; the
#                     most precise statement of the viability law.
#   Conant-Ashby 1970 (IEEE T-SMC; "Every Good Regulator of a
#                     System Must Be a Model of That System") —
#                     the foundational theorem the parametric form
#                     instantiates at the viable altitude.
#   Ashby 1952        (Design for a Brain; Wiley) — the homeostat;
#                     the four-unit electromechanical proof of
#                     ultrastable random reorganisation; Read A's
#                     load-bearing prior art.
#   Cybersyn          (Chile, 1971-1973) — VSM deployed at the
#                     political-economic altitude; the substrate-
#                     political precedent.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/cyberpunk-viable.md §3.1 (Read A
#               homeostat — held), §3.2 (Read B recursive viability
